~ stone_1

Unknown: Somebody went to the trouble of a headstone. The least I can do is read it. [ID:HINT_STONE_1]

=> END

~ stone_2

Unknown: That gravestone. There's lettering on it, what's left of it. [ID:HINT_STONE_2]

=> END

~ stone_3

Unknown: The gravestone, up close. The name, and the words under it. [ID:HINT_STONE_3]

=> END

~ gravedigger_1

Unknown: Somebody dug the grave I climbed out of. Graves don't dig themselves. [ID:HINT_GRAVEDIGGER_1]

=> END

~ gravedigger_2

Unknown: There was a gate west of my grave. Somebody's working there. [ID:HINT_GRAVEDIGGER_2]

=> END

~ gravedigger_3

Unknown: West of the grave, at the gate. Talk to the Gravedigger. [ID:HINT_GRAVEDIGGER_3]

=> END

~ register_1

Unknown: A gravedigger keeps records. Someone has to. [ID:HINT_REGISTER_1]

=> END

~ register_2

Unknown: His lodge, by the gate. There was a book on a lectern. [ID:HINT_REGISTER_2]

=> END

~ register_3

Unknown: In the Gravedigger's lodge, read the book on the lectern. [ID:HINT_REGISTER_3]

=> END

~ ossuary_key_1

Unknown: The book said which key. I only have to believe it. [ID:HINT_OSSUARY_KEY_1]

=> END

~ ossuary_key_2

Unknown: Key thirteen, on the wall in the lodge. [ID:HINT_OSSUARY_KEY_2]

=> END

~ ossuary_key_3

Unknown: Take key thirteen from the key wall in the lodge. [ID:HINT_OSSUARY_KEY_3]

=> END

~ crypt_1

Unknown: A key is only interesting next to a lock. [ID:HINT_CRYPT_1]

=> END

~ crypt_2

Unknown: The crypt steps at the gate, under the chapel. [ID:HINT_CRYPT_2]

=> END

~ crypt_3

Unknown: Use the ossuary key on the crypt steps by the gate. [ID:HINT_CRYPT_3]

=> END

~ glass_1

Unknown: The crow brought its treasures somewhere down here. [ID:HINT_GLASS_1]

=> END

~ glass_2

Unknown: High up in the ossuary, on the ledge. A nest. [ID:HINT_GLASS_2]

=> END

~ glass_3

Unknown: Take the glass from the crow's nest in the ossuary. [ID:HINT_GLASS_3]

=> END

~ mend_1

Unknown: A lantern glass is wasted in my hands. [ID:HINT_MEND_1]

=> END

~ mend_2

Unknown: The Gravedigger lost exactly this. [ID:HINT_MEND_2]

=> END

~ mend_3

Unknown: Give the lantern glass to the Gravedigger. [ID:HINT_MEND_3]

=> END

~ sister_1

Unknown: The cathedral had more doors than the one I came in by. [ID:HINT_SISTER_1]

=> END

~ sister_2

Unknown: An arch in the nave's aisle, with moonlight beyond. Someone's out there. [ID:HINT_SISTER_2]

=> END

~ sister_3

Unknown: Through the arch in the nave, to the cloister. Talk to the Sister. [ID:HINT_SISTER_3]

=> END

~ dove_1

Unknown: The stone was signed by a dove. The Sister has been here a long time. [ID:HINT_DOVE_1]

=> END

~ dove_2

Unknown: Ask the Sister whether she knew anyone called the dove. [ID:HINT_DOVE_2]

=> END

~ dove_3

Unknown: Ask the Sister about the dove. [ID:HINT_DOVE_3]

=> END

~ book_request_1

Unknown: Those doors in the nave lead to the city. Somebody holds the key. [ID:HINT_BOOK_REQUEST_1]

=> END

~ book_request_2

Unknown: The Sister has the key. Tell her I need to get into the city. [ID:HINT_BOOK_REQUEST_2]

=> END

~ book_request_3

Unknown: Ask the Sister about getting into the city. [ID:HINT_BOOK_REQUEST_3]

=> END

~ singer_1

Unknown: The dove's hymn book is up in the choir loft. In the dark. [ID:HINT_SINGER_1]

=> END

~ singer_2

Unknown: The turret stair in the cloister. I'll need the Gravedigger's lantern to see. [ID:HINT_SINGER_2]

=> END

~ singer_3

Unknown: With the lantern, climb the turret to the choir loft and touch the hymn book. [ID:HINT_SINGER_3]

=> END

~ book_1

Unknown: That book has done remembering for me. Now it should go to someone who'll keep it. [ID:HINT_BOOK_1]

=> END

~ book_2

Unknown: The hymn book, on its stand in the loft. [ID:HINT_BOOK_2]

=> END

~ book_3

Unknown: Take the hymn book from its stand. [ID:HINT_BOOK_3]

=> END

~ west_key_1

Unknown: The Sister wanted something of hers. I have it. [ID:HINT_WEST_KEY_1]

=> END

~ west_key_2

Unknown: Give the Sister the hymn book. [ID:HINT_WEST_KEY_2]

=> END

~ west_key_3

Unknown: Give the hymn book to the Sister in the cloister. [ID:HINT_WEST_KEY_3]

=> END

~ doors_1

Unknown: A key, and a city on the other side of a door. [ID:HINT_DOORS_1]

=> END

~ doors_2

Unknown: The great doors, on the right of the nave. [ID:HINT_DOORS_2]

=> END

~ doors_3

Unknown: Use the west door key on the great doors in the nave. [ID:HINT_DOORS_3]

=> END

~ ch1_square_1

Unknown: The doors are open. Whoever I was, he walked these streets. [ID:HINT_CH1_SQUARE_1]

=> END

~ ch1_square_2

Unknown: Through the great doors in the nave, into the city. [ID:HINT_CH1_SQUARE_2]

=> END

~ ch1_square_3

Unknown: Use the great doors in the nave. [ID:HINT_CH1_SQUARE_3]

=> END

~ crier_1

Unknown: Somebody's shouting in the square. News might help. [ID:HINT_CRIER_1]

=> END

~ crier_2

Unknown: The Crier, on his platform in the cathedral square. [ID:HINT_CRIER_2]

=> END

~ crier_3

Unknown: Talk to the Crier in the square. [ID:HINT_CRIER_3]

=> END

~ lamplighter_1

Unknown: The lamp street. Someone's lighting lamps that don't light. [ID:HINT_LAMPLIGHTER_1]

=> END

~ lamplighter_2

Unknown: Left of the square, the street of lamps. Talk to the Lamplighter. [ID:HINT_LAMPLIGHTER_2]

=> END

~ lamplighter_3

Unknown: Talk to the Lamplighter on the street of lamps. [ID:HINT_LAMPLIGHTER_3]

=> END

~ clockmaker_1

Unknown: A stopped clock, and somebody keeping it ready. [ID:HINT_CLOCKMAKER_1]

=> END

~ clockmaker_2

Unknown: Past the market and over the bridge, at the foot of the tower. [ID:HINT_CLOCKMAKER_2]

=> END

~ clockmaker_3

Unknown: Talk to the Clockmaker under the clock tower. [ID:HINT_CLOCKMAKER_3]

=> END

~ wedding_1

Unknown: The saint in the market wears a ribbon somebody tied for a reason. [ID:HINT_WEDDING_1]

=> END

~ wedding_2

Unknown: Touch the ribbon on the weeping saint in the market. [ID:HINT_WEDDING_2]

=> END

~ wedding_3

Unknown: Use the ribbon on the saint's wrist, in the market square. [ID:HINT_WEDDING_3]

=> END

~ candle_1

Unknown: The wedding went up the alley, to the tavern. Something of it might still be there. [ID:HINT_CANDLE_1]

=> END

~ candle_2

Unknown: The tavern, up the alley. The mantel. [ID:HINT_CANDLE_2]

=> END

~ candle_3

Unknown: Take the candle stub from the tavern mantel. [ID:HINT_CANDLE_3]

=> END

~ mathis_1

Unknown: A wedding candle, and a man who wants one warm flame. [ID:HINT_MATHIS_1]

=> END

~ mathis_2

Unknown: Give the wedding candle to the Lamplighter. [ID:HINT_MATHIS_2]

=> END

~ mathis_3

Unknown: Give the candle to the Lamplighter on the street of lamps. [ID:HINT_MATHIS_3]

=> END

~ winding_key_1

Unknown: The Clockmaker pawned his key. The Broker deals in stories, not money. [ID:HINT_WINDING_KEY_1]

=> END

~ winding_key_2

Unknown: The Broker wants something with a story in it. I have a lantern someone mended for a stranger. [ID:HINT_WINDING_KEY_2]

=> END

~ winding_key_3

Unknown: Give the Gravedigger's lantern to the Broker in his shop. [ID:HINT_WINDING_KEY_3]

=> END

~ eleven_1

Unknown: The clock has to be set to the hour it stopped. Somebody announced that hour once. [ID:HINT_ELEVEN_1]

=> END

~ eleven_2

Unknown: The Crier's last headline. Or the edicts in the alley. [ID:HINT_ELEVEN_2]

=> END

~ eleven_3

Unknown: Ask the Crier for the latest news. [ID:HINT_ELEVEN_3]

=> END

~ apprentice_1

Unknown: The clock remembers better than the Clockmaker, he said. [ID:HINT_APPRENTICE_1]

=> END

~ apprentice_2

Unknown: Inside the clock, with the warm lamp. Touch the escapement. [ID:HINT_APPRENTICE_2]

=> END

~ apprentice_3

Unknown: With the warm lamp, go into the clock and use the escapement. [ID:HINT_APPRENTICE_3]

=> END

~ escapement_1

Unknown: I know where the pin goes now. [ID:HINT_ESCAPEMENT_1]

=> END

~ escapement_2

Unknown: The escapement, inside the clock. Third tooth. [ID:HINT_ESCAPEMENT_2]

=> END

~ escapement_3

Unknown: Use the escapement again: the pin on the third tooth. [ID:HINT_ESCAPEMENT_3]

=> END

~ wound_1

Unknown: The clock needs its key turned. [ID:HINT_WOUND_1]

=> END

~ wound_2

Unknown: The winding post, beside the escapement. [ID:HINT_WOUND_2]

=> END

~ wound_3

Unknown: Use the winding key on the winding post. [ID:HINT_WOUND_3]

=> END

~ strike_1

Unknown: Behind the face, the hands. Eleven bells. [ID:HINT_STRIKE_1]

=> END

~ strike_2

Unknown: Climb the ladder to the clock face and set the hands. [ID:HINT_STRIKE_2]

=> END

~ strike_3

Unknown: Behind the clock face, use the hands. [ID:HINT_STRIKE_3]

=> END

~ lower_gate_1

Unknown: The clock struck, and something below opened. [ID:HINT_LOWER_GATE_1]

=> END

~ lower_gate_2

Unknown: Down the stair from the tower square, to the lower gate. [ID:HINT_LOWER_GATE_2]

=> END

~ lower_gate_3

Unknown: Go through the open portcullis at the lower gate. [ID:HINT_LOWER_GATE_3]

=> END

~ none

Unknown: Nothing pulls at me right now. The rest of me is still out there, somewhere. [ID:HINT_NONE_1]

=> END
